  "shared_conditions": [
    "Exact real arithmetic; positive epsilon and positive feature/head widths. The scaled residual case requires positive integer depth.",
    "Four streams, separate attention and SwiGLU sublayers, input and output Peri-RMS, normalized embedding, and twice-sigmoid write gates.",
    "Routing logits may depend on the current streams. The paper finite Sinkhorn algorithm performs twenty column-then-row cycles, without denominator regularization. Positivity and final row normalization suffice; exact double stochasticity is not assumed.",
    "Q/K RMS and rotary SSMax retain log(N), with the two requested attention gains as separate specializations. Mean collapse precedes the existing final RMS; its output RMS is at most one for either residual coefficient."
  ],
  "limitations": [
